      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sheriff Samuel: \"That group out there with the tan lines and new slang, Jimmy—they didn't deserve it. Ain't nobody in this town should be running off their feet till no one’s left us here.\"\n\nGritty eyes settle on his companion, noting the visible strain in Jimmy’s shoulders as he tugs a cheap leather apron. The aging wood and paint of the table groan under the tension, a silent orchestra of unease.\n\nJimmy, fumbling with a rusted cash register, lets out a pained chuckle, specks of dust flying from his rough hands in a whirl of remorse. He slams the drawer closed, his knuckles striking the metal with the force of a thrown punch.\n\nJimmy: \"Don’t get it twisted, Samuel. Them's the same rough hills we always settled until when. But hell, them got votes now, and we don't. Nothing sticks, not on solid ground like it used to. You lot, you thought you owned this place. Hell even led us through hell before.\"\n\nSheriff Samuel crumples some stale roll-towel, his gruff baritone squelching like soured dough. He takes a sharp, reluctant breath, savoring the moment before he bares",
      "source": "target",
